# SHA-256 of every PSO input table in this case directory.
#
# Digests are over LF-NORMALISED bytes (this repo checks out CRLF on Windows -- see
# .gitattributes), so they are identical on every platform.
#
# Verify:     python pso/tools/manifest.py --case-dir pso/texas7k2030_ercot_perunit
#             (or `pytest pso/test_manifest.py`, which always runs -- no data bundle needed)
# Regenerate: python pso/tools/manifest.py --case-dir pso/texas7k2030_ercot_perunit --write
#             (written automatically at the end of every build_texas7k_case.py run)
#
# SCOPE: this proves the tables have not been altered since they were built. It does NOT prove
# they were built from the right constants -- only test_rebuild_reproduces_every_committed_table
# does that, and it needs the gitignored source bundle.
#
